lags":0,"comment_count":3,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"wmoxam","user_is_author":false,"tags":["video","web"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/4ysjy0","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/4ysjy0/web_will_die_when_oop_dies_zed_shaw"},{"short_id":"ci7oui","created_at":"2012-10-04T23:29:46.000-05:00","title":"Why the future doesn't need us (Bill Joy, 2000)","url":"http://www.wired.com/wired/archive/8.04/joy_pr.html","score":3,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"jcs","user_is_author":false,"tags":["philosophy","science"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/ci7oui","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/ci7oui/why_future_doesn_t_need_us_bill_joy_2000"},{"short_id":"hnqhne","created_at":"2012-10-04T17:27:13.000-05:00","title":"LinkedIn Moves from Rails to Node","url":"http://highscalability.com/blog/2012/10/4/linkedin-moved-from-rails-to-node-27-servers-cut-and-up-to-2.html","score":5,"flags":4,"comment_count":8,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"benwoodall","user_is_author":false,"tags":["javascript","ruby","scaling"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/hnqhne","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/hnqhne/linkedin_moves_from_rails_node"},{"short_id":"sjpw4h","created_at":"2012-10-04T17:15:06.000-05:00","title":"Broadcom Teaches Kids to Program in an Hour Using Raspberry Pi","url":"http://mashable.com/2012/10/04/broadcom-teaches-kids-to-program-using-raspberry-pi/","score":4,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"benwoodall","user_is_author":false,"tags":["compsci","hardware"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/sjpw4h","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/sjpw4h/broadcom_teaches_kids_program_hour_using"},{"short_id":"k19u1k","created_at":"2012-10-04T15:22:06.000-05:00","title":"Enumerator: Ruby’s Versatile Iterator","url":"http://blog.carbonfive.com/2012/10/02/enumerator-rubys-versatile-iterator/","score":4,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"benwoodall","user_is_author":false,"tags":["ruby"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/k19u1k","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/k19u1k/enumerator_ruby_s_versatile_iterator"},{"short_id":"11wkuh","created_at":"2012-10-04T13:06:31.000-05:00","title":"node.js stream handbook","url":"https://github.com/substack/stream-handbook","score":10,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"eigenjoy","user_is_author":false,"tags":["javascript"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/11wkuh","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/11wkuh/node_js_stream_handbook"},{"short_id":"g0nxrf","created_at":"2012-10-04T12:04:37.000-05:00","title":"We have the ability to cache and display story text; should we?","url":"","score":6,"flags":0,"comment_count":9,"description":"\u003cp\u003eSomething I often wanted to see on Hacker News was an automatic link to a cached copy of a submission, so when the site goes down, there's still something to read.  I thought about taking it one step further and making the text of the article automatically available.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA user \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/jcs/lobsters/issues/27\" rel=\"ugc\"\u003erecently requested\u003c/a\u003e story texts be made available through RSS and it made me think about doing this some more, so I \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/jcs/lobsters/commit/67b61b5a9fd77efbe034cfc344ea1fc67ff95f55\" rel=\"ugc\"\u003ecoded up\u003c/a\u003e the feature on a branch.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen a story is submitted, it would cache the text (using \u003ca href=\"http://diffbot.com\" rel=\"ugc\"\u003eDiffbot\u003c/a\u003e) and show it as a collapsed block in the story:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"http://i.imgur.com/Dmna6.png\" rel=\"ugc\"\u003ehttp://i.imgur.com/Dmna6.png\u003c/a\u003e -\u0026gt; \u003ca href=\"http://i.imgur.com/NW8eo.png\" rel=\"ugc\"\u003ehttp://i.imgur.com/NW8eo.png\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis text would be displayed as the RSS text, as well as be included in the Sphinx index so that articles could be found through the \u003ca href=\"/search\" rel=\"ugc\"\u003esearch engine\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOf course there are copyright concerns caching the pages of others, not to mention the decreased traffic and possible ad revenue that might result from people reading the story here or through RSS rather than clicking through. Diffbot doesn't seem to honor robots.txt or meta tags that would otherwise restrict Google or Wayback Machine's archiving.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat do you guys think?\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"Something I often wanted to see on Hacker News was an automatic link to a cached copy of a submission, so when the site goes down, there's still something to read.  I thought about taking it one step further and making the text of the article automatically available.\r\n\r\nA user [recently requested](https://github.com/jcs/lobsters/issues/27) story texts be made available through RSS and it made me think about doing this some more, so I [coded up](https://github.com/jcs/lobsters/commit/67b61b5a9fd77efbe034cfc344ea1fc67ff95f55) the feature on a branch.\r\n\r\nWhen a story is submitted, it would cache the text (using [Diffbot](http://diffbot.com)) and show it as a collapsed block in the story:\r\n\r\nhttp://i.imgur.com/Dmna6.png -\u003e http://i.imgur.com/NW8eo.png\r\n\r\nThis text would be displayed as the RSS text, as well as be included in the Sphinx index so that articles could be found through the [search engine](/search).\r\n\r\nOf course there are copyright concerns caching the pages of others, not to mention the decreased traffic and possible ad revenue that might result from people reading the story here or through RSS rather than clicking through. Diffbot doesn't seem to honor robots.txt or meta tags that would otherwise restrict Google or Wayback Machine's archiving.\r\n\r\nWhat do you guys think?","submitter_user":"jcs","user_is_author":false,"tags":["law","meta"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/g0nxrf","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/g0nxrf/we_have_ability_cache_display_story_text"},{"short_id":"dm2agb","created_at":"2012-10-04T12:00:37.000-05:00","title":"LibEtPan: a portable mail framework","url":"http://www.etpan.org/","score":4,"flags":0,"comment_count":1,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"tenderlove","user_is_author":false,"tags":["c"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/dm2agb","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/dm2agb/libetpan_portable_mail_framework"},{"short_id":"twah8c","created_at":"2012-10-04T11:22:06.000-05:00","title":"Show Lobsters: A Better Random (Wikipedia Link Generator)","url":"https://github.com/benolee/abetterrandom.herokuapp.com","score":3,"flags":1,"comment_count":3,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"benolee","user_is_author":false,"tags":["ruby","web"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/twah8c","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/twah8c/show_lobsters_better_random_wikipedia"},{"short_id":"qftilv","created_at":"2012-10-04T07:56:53.000-05:00","title":"LEGO Great Ball Contraption (GBC) Layout 2012.9","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sUtS52lqL5w","score":1,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"tobym","user_is_author":false,"tags":["hardware","video"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/qftilv","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/qftilv/lego_great_ball_contraption_gbc_layout"},{"short_id":"4wdryd","created_at":"2012-10-04T04:43:47.000-05:00","title":"Open Source's Final Frontier","url":"http://spectrum.ieee.org/tech-talk/at-work/innovation/opensource-hardware-summit","score":2,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"iamelgringo","user_is_author":false,"tags":["hardware"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/4wdryd","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/4wd